---
import StaticPage from '../layouts/StaticPage.astro';
---

<StaticPage
  title="Corrections Policy"
  description="How we handle errors, updates, and corrections to published stories."
  canonicalPath="/corrections-policy/"
  updated="September 2026"
>
  <p>
    We take accuracy seriously. When we get something wrong, we correct it promptly,
    transparently, and in a way that is easy for readers to find.
  </p>

  <h2>Reporting an error</h2>
  <p>
    If you believe a story contains an error, please contact us through our{' '}
    <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page with the story headline, the specific
    issue, and any supporting information.
  </p>

  <h2>How we correct</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Minor fixes</strong> (typos, formatting) are made without a formal correction notice.</li>
    <li><strong>Substantive corrections</strong> update the story body and add a dated correction note explaining what changed and why.</li>
    <li><strong>Major errors</strong> that change the meaning of a story are corrected, noted prominently, and reflected in the story's "Updated" timestamp.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Updates vs. corrections</h2>
  <p>
    An <em>update</em> adds new, accurate information as a story develops. A{' '}
    <em>correction</em> fixes something that was wrong. Both are reflected in the
    story's published and updated timestamps.
  </p>

  <h2>Retractions</h2>
  <p>
    If a story is fundamentally flawed, we will retract it, replace the body with a
    retraction notice explaining why, and preserve the original URL so the record
    remains accessible.
  </p>
</StaticPage>
